docs {
  # Set Our Price and Enable a Plan
  
  Set `dataPlanId` in the active Bruno environment to the plan's database `id`
  returned by the admin list request.
  
  `networkPrice` and `providerPrice` come from SMEAPI, SME Plug, Autopilot,
  UjayData, Ogdams, 2Fast, or VTpass and cannot be changed here. `ourPrice`,
  `vendorPrice`, `dataType`, `isEnabled`, `isHot`, display overrides, `note`,
  and delivery controls belong to BillXpress and are preserved during
  synchronization.
  
  `ourPrice` is the fixed selling price for normal app users. `vendorPrice` is
  the fixed selling price for active vendors/API users.

  ## Hot Plans

  Set `isHot` when admin wants a plan to appear in the app's Hot tab:

  ```json
  {
    "isHot": true
  }
  ```

  Remove it from Hot with:

  ```json
  {
    "isHot": false
  }
  ```

  The plan still needs `isEnabled=true` before customers can see or buy it.

  ## Customer Display Overrides And Note

  Use display override fields when the provider's plan text is unclear or not
  how BillXpress wants to show it in the app:

  ```json
  {
    "displayNetwork": "MTN",
    "displayName": "MTN 1GB Daily Special",
    "displayDataType": "Daily",
    "displayValidity": "1 Day",
    "displayValidityDays": 1,
    "note": "Do not buy this plan if you are owing data."
  }
  ```

  These fields change only what customers receive on:

  ```txt
  GET /api/v1/services/data/plans
  ```

  They do not change the provider plan ID, provider code, provider name, cost,
  route, or any value used to complete the actual purchase.

  Clear a display override or note with `null` or an empty string:

  ```json
  {
    "displayName": null,
    "note": ""
  }
  ```

  ## Hosted SIM vs Provider Wallet Cost

  Use `fulfillmentRoute` to control which cost is used for markup/profit:

  ```json
  {
    "fulfillmentRoute": "network"
  }
  ```

  Uses `networkPrice` when it exists. This is for plans BillXpress fulfills from
  its own SIM/network stock.

  ```json
  {
    "fulfillmentRoute": "provider"
  }
  ```

  Uses `providerPrice` when it exists. This is for plans sold from provider
  wallet/API balance.

  For provider/API plans, set `fulfillmentRoute` to `provider`; otherwise profit
  can be calculated against the network price instead of the real provider
  charge. The older `allowHostedSim` field is still supported directly:
  `true` means network, and `false` means provider.
  
  ## Fixed Price
  
  ```json
  {
    "ourPrice": 450,
    "vendorPrice": 430,
    "isEnabled": true
  }
  ```
  
  `ourPrice` becomes the exact normal-user selling price. `vendorPrice` becomes
  the exact vendor/API selling price. No percentage is added for the audience
  whose fixed price is set.
  
  ## Percentage Fallback
  
  ```json
  {
    "ourPrice": null,
    "vendorPrice": null,
    "isEnabled": true
  }
  ```
  
  Clearing `ourPrice` restores normal-user tier/percentage pricing. Clearing
  `vendorPrice` restores vendor tier/percentage pricing. The plan can remain
  enabled.
  
  The backend rejects enabling a provider-unavailable plan.
  
  To hide a plan:
  
  ```json
  {
    "isEnabled": false
  }
  ```
}
